- op: discuss  # 4321
  at: '2026-08-13T18:58:32Z'  # 4321
  by: agent  # 4321
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4321
  clock: 8  # 4321
  nonce: '4321'  # 4321
  message: "CORRECTION TO THE FORK POSTED ABOVE — DO NOT DECIDE ON THAT FRAMING. Measured\nsince posting it: the packaging-scope option does NOT deliver what it promised.\nIt peels the FIRST blocker and exposes a SECOND one behind it.\n\nINSTRUMENT: production's own compute_boundary_coverage, with production's\nargument shapes, over a real self-survey (152,154 edges, cached from today's\nmerged tree). Simulating the packaging-scope fix (bash excluded from the\nproduction-scoped edge list):\n\n    production-scoped (today):   complete=False\n        reason: language(s) bash made calls but have no I/O catalog\n    ...with bash EXCLUDED:       complete=False\n        reason: supported language(s) elixir, go, java, rust, swift were\n        analyzed but produced no call edges, so their I/O is invisible\n\nThose five languages are FIXTURE-ONLY in this repo — every tracked .ex/.go/\n.java/.rs/.swift file (1/4/3/3/3) lives under a test or fixture directory.\nThey read as \"present and taint-supported\" because the language census walks\nALL NODES unscoped (cli.py:5305-5309) while the coverage check walks\nPRODUCTION-SCOPED edges. That incoherence is filed as its own invariant\n(INV — census/coverage population mismatch, INV-motos shape).\n\nTHREE INSTRUMENT VERSIONS WERE NEEDED, and version 2 is the one worth\nrecording: v1 passed io-catalogue languages where production passes\ntaint-supported ones and produced obvious nonsense (\"python has no I/O\ncatalog\"); v2 passed supported_present and produced a PLAUSIBLE wrong answer\n(a different blocker list) that could have shipped; v3 rebuilt per_lang_sinks\nfrom the taint catalogue the way cli.py does. Only the nonsense of v1 forced\nthe re-check that caught v2.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE DECISION. Neither option in the fork above is decidable\nyet, because the packaging-scope route's true cost is the WHOLE BLOCKER STACK,\nnot one blocker, and the stack has never been enumerated. A blocker-stack\ncensus over the cached survey is being run now and will be posted on this\nthread; the decision package (scope statement vs accept-and-disclose, with the\nstack priced) follows it.\n\nALSO FROM THE OWNER DISCUSSION, filed separately rather than folded in here:\nthe self-proof does not state its own SCOPE. All 18 claims declare python\ncmd_* sources — the installed CLI. Nothing covers running this repo's tests\n(six conftest.py files execute AT COLLECTION), hooks (32 shell files), CI, or\nthe rust-analyzer backend executing an analysed repo's build.rs. WI-bifob's\ndefault DISCARDS test-sourced flows — right for the shipped-tool threat model,\nand the artifact never says that is the model it serves."  # 4321
- op: discuss  # cf3b
  at: '2026-08-13T19:01:40Z'  # cf3b
  by: agent  # cf3b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cf3b
  clock: 9  # cf3b
  nonce: cf3b  # cf3b
  message: "BLOCKER-STACK CENSUS, as promised above. Method: each coverage layer's own\nfunction called DIRECTLY on the simulated substrate (compute_boundary_coverage\nshort-circuits, so its `reason` only ever names the front blocker). Substrate =\nproduction-scoped edges, bash excluded, census made coherent (the INV-sarum fix\nin its shipped-tool direction). CLI baseline re-confirmed first on today's\nmerged tree: 18/18 inconclusive, all on bash.\n\nTHE STACK IS FOUR LAYERS DEEP:\n\n  1. bash census blocker         (today's 18/18; the packaging-scope question)\n  2. fixture-only languages      (INV-sarum: elixir/go/java/rust/swift — a\n                                  census incoherence, not real blindness)\n  3. OPAQUE LAUNCH SITES x3      os.execv, subprocess.Popen, subprocess.run\n  4. UNCATALOGUED MODULES x134   argparse, hashlib, tarfile/zipfile, itertools,\n                                  ... (mostly stdlib; some garbage hints like\n                                  'file'/'document'/'caches', and\n                                  hypergumbo_core itself — the population is\n                                  noisy and needs triage before it is a work\n                                  estimate)\n\nmethod-starved modules: 0 on this substrate.\n\nLAYER 3 IS THE IMPORTANT ONE, because it is STRUCTURAL and cannot be drained\nby catalogue work: hypergumbo genuinely launches external programs (git for\nsketch, pip/rustup for installs), and what a launched program does is\ninvisible by construction. Under today's gate, any launch blocks every\nconfirm. So even after ALL catalogue work, the self-proof cannot reach rc 0.\n\nAND THE RESOLUTION FOR IT ALREADY EXISTS AS OF TODAY. ADR-0016 §4's fourth\nverdict was SPECIFIED for exactly this consumer — \"Confirmed with caveats:\nconsistent, but OPAQUE BOUNDARIES exist that could not be verified\" — and the\nrc-3 / caveats machinery landed today for INV-pojib with a `kind` axis built\nto take a second kind. The opaque-boundary kind is the ORIGINAL spec'd\nconsumer, noted as not-yet-implemented in today's ADR amendment.\n\nCONSEQUENCE, and it reframes the whole decision: THE SELF-PROOF'S HONEST\nTERMINAL STATE IS rc 3, NOT rc 0. Fully drained, it would read\n\"18/18 confirmed_with_caveats\" carrying BOTH caveat kinds — the zone-barrier\nsanitizer (repo-supplied, already forces rc 3 by today's INV-pojib change) and\nthe disclosed opaque launches. That is an honest, machine-checkable artifact:\n\"no exfiltration flow found, GIVEN these declared wrappers and MODULO these\nthree named launch sites.\" rc 0 was never on the table for a tool that shells\nout to git.\n\nPRICED PATH TO THAT STATE (each its own revertable PR):\n  a. INV-sarum census coherence        small, direction pending WI-kozos\n  b. bash: packaging-scope OR accept   the original fork, now honestly sized\n  c. opaque-boundary caveat kind       small-medium; the machinery exists,\n                                       the kind + tests + ADR note are new\n  d. layer-4 triage + stdlib rows      the LARGE one; 134 modules, noisy,\n                                       stdlib-scoped work is legitimate by\n                                       design (ADR-0016 §27) but unbounded\n                                       until triaged. NOT costed here.\n  e. WI-kozos scope statement          independent; should land regardless.\n\nOption (d)/accept-and-disclose remains available at every step and gets\ncheaper to justify as the residual shrinks and is named."  # cf3b
